{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"pushdown automaton pushdown automaton","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md","fileName":"Pushdown Automaton.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Pushdown Automaton","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 22:54\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Context-Free Languages and Parsing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Context-Free Languages and Parsing","Context-Free Language","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"pushdown automaton pushdown automaton","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md","fileName":"Pushdown Automaton.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Pushdown Automaton","heading":"Pushdown Automaton","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A pushdown automaton is a finite-state machine augmented by a stack. A transition may consume an input symbol or ε, pop a string from the stack, push a replacement string, and change state.\n\nThe stack supplies unbounded last-in-first-out memory for nested structure. Pushdown automata accept exactly the [[Context-Free Language|context-free languages]], and a grammar can be simulated by pushing its start symbol, expanding nonterminals, and matching terminals against the input.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Context-Free Languages and Parsing","Context-Free Language","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"pushdown automaton pushdown automaton","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Pushdown Automaton.md","fileName":"Pushdown Automaton.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Pushdown Automaton","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Context-Free Languages and Parsing","Context-Free Language","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}